{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f75921cd9023e497","name":"Canyon Krayt Dragon","source":{"id":"source:reference-f75921cd9023e497","title":"Canyon Krayt Dragon","revision":18876,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:54:02Z","sha256":"3061347a65997130fb8a3befa70615350a1ec1fe59add82306cb14ab2f34016a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18876","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Canyon%20Krayt%20Dragon&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f75921cd9023e497","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Canyon Krayt Dragons are smaller versions of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Krayt Dragon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Krayt_Dragon","referenceId":"reference:9e2806192a3a120a"},", but still immense monsters nonetheless. Canyon Krayt Dragons prowl the craggy mountains that border the Jundland Wastes of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tatooine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tatooine","referenceId":"reference:a1b911e88e4876e1"},". Single-minded and ferocious, the only thing a Canyon Krayt Dragon fears is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Greater Dragon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Greater_Dragon?action=edit&redlink=1"},"; sometimes these two titanic beasts clash when one strays into the other's territory. Canyon Dragons are weaker than Greater Dragons, but their smaller size works well in the twisting ravines and gullies of their lair, allowing them to entrap herds of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Banthas"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Banthas"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Eopies"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Eopies"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rontos"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rontos"}," with little more than ruthless predatory instinct and determination.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Canyon Krayt Dragons also have 1d4+4 of the same \"",{"tag":"a","children":["Krayt Dragon Pearls"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Krayt_Dragon_Pearls"},"\" in their stomachs as their greater cousins do and are considered slightly easier prey for hunters. That said, killing a Canyon Krayt Dragon is a remarkably dangerous task- most treasure seekers prefer to locate a dying or recently deceased Canyon Krayt Dragon to loot the stomach without facing the risk of having to go down its mouth the hard way.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Canyon Krayt Dragon Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["As befitting their name, Canyon Krayt Dragons are likely to be encountered in the cliffs and winding canyons that surround the immense dunes of Tatooine's Jundland Wastes. Because most of the indigenous creatures on that planet live in the relative \"safety\" of these rocky crags, the Canyon Krayt Dragon has plenty of prey to devour, making it dangerous for anyone who thinks they can stay out of harm's way by taking to the mesas and cliffs.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because of the huge amount of food they require, Canyon Krayt Dragons stalk herds of animals, such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Banthas"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Banthas"},", making it hazardous for characters to be near such a group for a long period of time. However, unless a Canyon Krayt Dragon is particularly hungry or aggravated, it is likely to ignore most Medium or smaller creatures (in other words, most heroes) unless they open fire or make a lot of noise or visual distractions. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tusken Raiders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tusken_Raiders"}," sometimes hunt juvenile Canyon Krayt Dragons, which provide tremendous amount of (ill-tasting) meat for their tribes, as well as raw materials for crafting items, or even shelter- the hide of a Canyon Krayt Dragon makes a fine canopy that repeals even the most intense heat from Tatooine's twin suns.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Canyon Krayt Dragon Statistics (CL 14)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal Desert ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 15 \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +6; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", Tremorsense, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +19\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 14 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 14), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 25, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 292, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 10, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 75\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 10 Squares; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Powerful Charge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Powerful_Charge","referenceId":"reference:d7f59c39adb93fd7"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Melee:"]}," Bite +24* (4d6+28) plus Devou